        "original_id": "c8260acd-7f38-5d65-85e1-85ea1e816bb8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, Roger Taylor, Taylor Hawkins, Lisa Carver\n- Groups/Bands: Sugarland, Soul Miner's Daughter, Jennifer Nettles Band, Foo Fighters, Queen\n- Songs: “Everyday America”, “Heaven for Everyone”\n- Organizations/Media: Planet Rock\n\nFacts:\n- Before Sugarland was formed, Jennifer Nettles fronted the Atlanta-based bands Soul Miner's Daughter and Jennifer Nettles Band.\n- Jennifer Nettles is best known as the lead singer of the duo Sugarland alongside Kristian Bush.\n- In 2005, Planet Rock listeners voted Roger Taylor the eighth-greatest drummer in classic rock history.\n- Roger Taylor was acclaimed by Foo Fighters drummer Taylor Hawkins as one of the most influential rock drummers of the 1970s and 1980s.\n- Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, and Lisa Carver wrote the song “Everyday America.”\n- Roger Taylor wrote the song “Heaven for Everyone.”",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
